00:47:11.620 --> 00:47:14.370
&gt;&gt; Well they come from
this listening thing.

00:47:15.450 --> 00:47:21.260
It's amazing how there's really
cool leading edge innovation and

00:47:21.260 --> 00:47:24.820
then there's just basic things that
we need to do right and better.

00:47:24.820 --> 00:47:29.190
And so,
most of our people focus on the latter,

00:47:29.190 --> 00:47:32.220
it's like the simple things like
this boarding thing I discussed.

00:47:32.220 --> 00:47:34.353
And so, getting input from that.

00:47:34.353 --> 00:47:38.836
On the innovation side, we started
what all of you around here know, but

00:47:38.836 --> 00:47:44.890
it isn't often as prevalent and big 100
year old industrial companies like mine.

00:47:44.890 --> 00:47:47.338
The concept of fast failure, right?

00:47:47.338 --> 00:47:52.180
Big companies employ people like you to
do all the analytics, and their and this,

00:47:52.180 --> 00:47:55.970
and all the studies, and
all these things about an idea.

00:47:55.970 --> 00:47:58.860
And you go months into it and
then somebody determines it's a go or

00:47:58.860 --> 00:48:04.480
a no go And then maybe you try it or
you don't, but you've wasted so much time.

00:48:04.480 --> 00:48:06.982
It's like somebody has kind of
a cool idea, it's like, go.

00:48:06.982 --> 00:48:09.546
And so we built a digital sort of group,

00:48:09.546 --> 00:48:13.824
it's actually a separate building,
just for many reasons, but

00:48:13.824 --> 00:48:18.960
you go in there and just the objective
in those rooms it's just bring ideas.

00:48:18.960 --> 00:48:22.517
Put them to, bring them up,
and see how well they scale.

00:48:22.517 --> 00:48:26.060
And it's amazing how many things take
hold, but how energetic that is.

00:48:26.060 --> 00:48:28.908
And now, in our company,
it's cool to come up with ideas.

00:48:28.908 --> 00:48:31.339
Before it was like, well,
management doesn't like it.

00:48:31.339 --> 00:48:32.255
You're talking back.

00:48:32.255 --> 00:48:36.013
So part of it is culture, but
also part of providing an environment, but

00:48:36.013 --> 00:48:38.491
more importantly acting
on that environment.

00:48:38.491 --> 00:48:40.566
So once getting back to proof,
not promise.

00:48:40.566 --> 00:48:43.517
It's like, yeah,
if you have an idea and it's coming up,

00:48:43.517 --> 00:48:47.356
I am taking you everywhere I go and
showing your mug everywhere, it's like,

00:48:47.356 --> 00:48:50.155
his idea, this the guy who did it,
this is what he does.

00:48:50.155 --> 00:48:53.085
I mean, we have so many wonderful
histories that we tell about our company.

00:48:53.085 --> 00:48:54.854
So creating that culture and

00:48:54.854 --> 00:48:58.686
all of you are probably more familiar
with it because if you live and

00:48:58.686 --> 00:49:03.192
work around here, it's easier to do
that in a smaller younger company.

00:49:03.192 --> 00:49:05.922
Hundred year old companies
just don't do that,

00:49:05.922 --> 00:49:09.129
might the tenure of my Workforce
the level of education.

00:49:09.129 --> 00:49:13.282
All of those things are subject but never
underestimate the power of human caring,

00:49:13.282 --> 00:49:16.488
human engagement and
human experience makes a big difference,

00:49:16.488 --> 00:49:19.528
especially when it comes time
