00:49:21.700 --> 00:49:24.753
&gt;&gt; Hi my name is Jorge Queto and
I'm a first year MBA.

00:49:24.753 --> 00:49:27.250
My question is related
to work culture as well.

00:49:27.250 --> 00:49:31.541
What do you think is necessary to create
a more inclusive work environment for

00:49:31.541 --> 00:49:36.294
Latinos, as well as for people from other
underepresented groups including women,

00:49:36.294 --> 00:49:39.810
black people, LGBTQ people,
and undocumented immigrants.

00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:43.340
&gt;&gt; Did we miss anybody on that list?

00:49:43.340 --> 00:49:51.308
Veterans, disabilities like autism.

00:49:51.308 --> 00:49:54.926
Biggest and best supporter I think of
Special Olympics that we come in united

00:49:54.926 --> 00:49:57.200
because I believe in that whole breadth.

00:49:57.200 --> 00:49:59.782
Yes, it's my heritage and
my natural asset.

00:49:59.782 --> 00:50:01.940
I'll tell you,
diversity inclusion, two words.

00:50:01.940 --> 00:50:04.271
Diversity and inclusions,
they're two different terms.

00:50:04.271 --> 00:50:11.590
Diversity has become, we've made progress,
it's numeric, metric-oriented progress.

00:50:11.590 --> 00:50:17.284
I have the largest percentage of female
pilots in the world in aviation.

00:50:17.284 --> 00:50:21.135
Yay, it's 8%.

00:50:21.135 --> 00:50:22.100
But it's the best.

00:50:22.100 --> 00:50:24.212
I relax, right, no?

00:50:24.212 --> 00:50:26.450
Diversity's is just not about numbers.

00:50:26.450 --> 00:50:29.200
How are my women of color, for instance?

00:50:29.200 --> 00:50:32.715
But more importantly,
back to the other word, inclusive.

00:50:32.715 --> 00:50:36.165
I go see my women pilots and
I say, hey, yay, did you hear,

00:50:36.165 --> 00:50:39.270
you're the largest
percentage in the industry.

00:50:39.270 --> 00:50:40.911
Do you think they celebrate that?

00:50:40.911 --> 00:50:44.967
No, because when I asked I said,
what else can we do better?

00:50:44.967 --> 00:50:47.187
There's always a list of things and

00:50:47.187 --> 00:50:51.450
those lists of things are on
the inclusive aspect of it, right?

00:50:51.450 --> 00:50:52.504
Am I involved?

00:50:52.504 --> 00:50:53.900
Do you value me?

00:50:53.900 --> 00:50:56.531
These microaggressions of stopping people.

00:50:56.531 --> 00:51:00.120
It's like do you know that women get
cut off in meetings more than anyone?

00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:03.887
And you tell it to a guys, he's like no,
it hasn't happened, watch.

00:51:03.887 --> 00:51:08.040
And you go back and watch,
it's like dang, we do things like that.

00:51:08.040 --> 00:51:11.252
And so part of the thing that we're doing,
and Latinos.

00:51:11.252 --> 00:51:15.341
Latinos, by the way,
the millennial thing we all talk about,

00:51:15.341 --> 00:51:21.150
guess what the demographic looks like very
soon of millennials versus boomers, right?

00:51:21.150 --> 00:51:22.757
Millennials bigger, next year.

00:51:22.757 --> 00:51:24.720
73 million versus 72 million.

00:51:24.720 --> 00:51:29.321
Guess what the percentage of millenials
are that are Latino in this country,

00:51:29.321 --> 00:51:30.183
almost half.

00:51:30.183 --> 00:51:34.580
So I don't go tell you you gotta do
this and you gotta hire Latinos.

00:51:34.580 --> 00:51:38.790
I tell you it is an economic force
that is a massive proportions.

00:51:38.790 --> 00:51:42.749
Why Dara from Uber and Dennis Mullemberg
were in the meeting with me,

00:51:42.749 --> 00:51:47.185
is because they recognize that it's
a A $2 plus trillion market, Latinos are,

00:51:47.185 --> 00:51:50.274
and 56 is in the transportation
leisure business.

00:51:50.274 --> 00:51:52.380
So it's a right market, right?

00:51:52.380 --> 00:51:55.815
Where you're all looking for growth and
for your companies and all the stuff,

00:51:55.815 --> 00:51:57.490
well, you go fish where the fish are.

00:51:57.490 --> 00:51:59.982
And the fish have a little
spicy salsa next to them.

00:51:59.982 --> 00:52:06.425
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] I can say that.

00:52:06.425 --> 00:52:11.470
But it comes across all cultures and
everything.

00:52:11.470 --> 00:52:13.480
There's just so much to be done.

00:52:13.480 --> 00:52:14.012
I'll tell you,

00:52:14.012 --> 00:52:17.350
and I'm talking about it tonight in
San Francisco with Women in the Workplace.

00:52:17.350 --> 00:52:19.351
My next mission is to some degree,

00:52:19.351 --> 00:52:23.294
because we have one of the highest
percentage of women in the workplace.

00:52:23.294 --> 00:52:25.260
Again, the numbers all work out for us.

00:52:25.260 --> 00:52:28.834
And a way, not the point,
harassment, sexual harassment for

00:52:28.834 --> 00:52:31.613
a flight attendant for
people is still an issue.

00:52:31.613 --> 00:52:35.420
There's still idiots that sit next
to people and think they can touch,

00:52:35.420 --> 00:52:38.920
think they can do and ask and
say things that they shouldn't.

00:52:38.920 --> 00:52:41.035
And there's still people
that sit next to someone and

00:52:41.035 --> 00:52:44.243
don't want to sit next to someone because
of their race, color, sex, or creed.

00:52:44.243 --> 00:52:47.070
Those people have no time,
nowhere, no business.

00:52:47.070 --> 00:52:50.536
You can go fly elsewhere because that's
just not something we're going to do.

00:52:50.536 --> 00:52:54.497
Hard to do in this market because I have
to remove them from the aircraft, right?

00:52:54.497 --> 00:52:55.977
And then we have that whole other issue.

00:52:55.977 --> 00:52:59.694
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] What else?

00:52:59.694 --> 00:53:06.128
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; So

00:53:06.128 --> 00:53:10.408
I'd like to close by doing a quick
lightning round if possible.

00:53:10.408 --> 00:53:11.350
&gt;&gt; Sure.

00:53:11.350 --> 00:53:14.086
&gt;&gt; So this or that style.

00:53:14.086 --> 00:53:15.069
Aisle or window?

00:53:19.288 --> 00:53:21.670
&gt;&gt; An aisle because if you sit
next to me you just get abused.

00:53:21.670 --> 00:53:25.874
I mean, people reach over, customers and
employees will reach over you,

00:53:25.874 --> 00:53:27.154
stand in front of you.

00:53:27.154 --> 00:53:30.211
So I always sit at the window so
I can just talk to people and

00:53:30.211 --> 00:53:33.030
not disrupt my fellow
flying person next to me.

00:53:33.030 --> 00:53:36.326
And yes I do fly my own
airline all the time.

00:53:36.326 --> 00:53:37.580
Gotta eat what you cook.

00:53:37.580 --> 00:53:39.496
Not all airline executives do that.

00:53:39.496 --> 00:53:41.765
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Coke or Pepsi?

00:53:41.765 --> 00:53:42.591
&gt;&gt; You know what?

00:53:42.591 --> 00:53:45.930
Coke was my last time, so
Classic Coke, no additives.

00:53:45.930 --> 00:53:49.076
I watch what goes into other products,
and so,

00:53:49.076 --> 00:53:52.703
the stuff in regular Coke is
at least God made, right?

00:53:52.703 --> 00:53:53.837
It's natural.

00:53:53.837 --> 00:53:54.860
It's sugar.

00:53:54.860 --> 00:53:57.088
&gt;&gt; Planes or trains?

00:53:57.088 --> 00:53:59.330
&gt;&gt; Yeah,
I got to go with my family, planes.

00:54:01.270 --> 00:54:03.286
&gt;&gt; Adventure or relaxation?

00:54:03.286 --> 00:54:04.687
&gt;&gt; God, adventure.

00:54:04.687 --> 00:54:06.080
[LAUGH] I don't know what that other word.

00:54:06.080 --> 00:54:07.398
I do know what that word is.

00:54:07.398 --> 00:54:10.000
And after I've done some
adventure something.

00:54:10.000 --> 00:54:11.520
Kardashians or The Bachelor?

00:54:11.520 --> 00:54:15.094
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I'd label that the fall of

00:54:15.094 --> 00:54:16.643
Western Civilization as we know it.

00:54:16.643 --> 00:54:22.940
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:54:22.940 --> 00:54:24.399
&gt;&gt; NorCal or SoCal?

00:54:24.399 --> 00:54:30.965
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] I'm a so cowboy.

00:54:30.965 --> 00:54:31.681
That's no question.

00:54:31.681 --> 00:54:32.556
I love it up here.

00:54:32.556 --> 00:54:35.358
I got engaged here,
I went running, walking, jogging.

00:54:35.358 --> 00:54:38.469
It's hilly,
I forget how hilly it is downtown, but

00:54:38.469 --> 00:54:42.030
the Saint Francis Hotel
is where I got engaged.

00:54:42.030 --> 00:54:43.269
So that always brings a lot of memory.

00:54:43.269 --> 00:54:45.664
The Carnoelon Room probably most
of you don't even remember,

00:54:45.664 --> 00:54:47.165
it used to be at the top of the BFA tower.

00:54:47.165 --> 00:54:50.365
&gt;&gt; That's when I started my way
through my, I thought I was so

00:54:50.365 --> 00:54:53.563
confident in my request to my
wife to join me in marriage but

00:54:53.563 --> 00:54:56.069
I couldn't get the two words out for
a while.

00:54:56.069 --> 00:54:58.340
[LAUGH] So
it's always be close in that regard.

00:54:58.340 --> 00:55:00.813
&gt;&gt; Then of course the last one,
Delta or American?

00:55:00.813 --> 00:55:03.272
No, I'm just kidding, you don't have to.

00:55:03.272 --> 00:55:06.686
It has been a pleasure speaking with you
Oscar, please join me in thanking him.

00:55:06.686 --> 00:55:08.723
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Great job.

00:55:08.723 --> 00:55:09.683
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:55:09.683 --> 00:55:14.672
[MUSIC]

